          </p>

          <p>
            Jackery's Explorer 1000 v2 is the most direct rival and, for a lot of buyers, the more pleasant one to own. It stores a little more energy, 1,070 Wh or about 910 Wh usable, in a lighter case. That gap matters more than it sounds when you are carrying the box from a car to a campsite or up from a basement during an outage. Where it gives ground is ceiling: continuous output stops at 1,500 W, there is no add-on battery, and the fastest wall charging has to be switched on in the app. If you are confident 1 kWh is your size, those limits rarely bite, and the simplicity is a feature.
