            Add EcoFlow's extra batteries and the capacity scales into the tens of kilowatt-hours; add its smart home panel or a transfer switch and the station powers selected house circuits directly. The trade-offs are real: at about 114 pounds it moves on wheels, not by hand, the panel connection needs a licensed electrician, and the full setup with panels and switchgear is a large outlay. But it is the most complete battery backup system either brand sells.
          </p>

          <p>
            Jackery's answer is its larger Explorer Plus systems, led by a roughly 5 kWh flagship designed around expansion batteries, 240 V output and a transfer switch for home use. Model names, capacities and bundles in this tier change frequently, so rather than quote figures we cannot pin down for every current variant, the table compares what each platform offers.
