          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            EcoFlow and Jackery both make good LFP power stations with roughly five-year warranties, so there is no wrong brand here, only the wrong fit. EcoFlow is the better buy when the station lives at home, you want the most output per size class, or you expect to add batteries, a smart panel or a solar array later; the Delta 3 Plus and Delta Pro 3 are its strongest arguments.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Jackery is the better buy when you will carry the station often and already know the size you need; the Explorer 1000 v2 and the single-box Explorer 2000 v2 are the lightest ways to get that capacity. Size your load first with the runtime rule, then let that answer pick the brand.
